[list]
[*]Fixed: with Outfit Stands Plus installed, a colonist could be sent to someone else's stand and take the clothes parked there. Each stand kept two owner lists, this mod's and Outfit Stands Plus's, and only one of them had a Set owner button at a time. An owner set through Outfit Stands Plus before the stand went into shift use stayed on the hidden list and kept that mod's "equip outfit" button for the stand, and one click swapped out the new owner's kit. Nothing on the stand could show or clear that entry.
[*]Every stand now has one owner list, set with this mod's Set owner in both modes, and Outfit Stands Plus follows it. A colonist who is a stand's only owner gets the Outfit Stands Plus button for it, on stands in shift use too, which suits a sleep stand since it holds their own clothes. A stand with several owners, or none, gives that button to nobody. Outfit Stands Plus's own Set owner no longer appears on these stands, and ours only offers colonists that mod would accept, so its adult and child stands stay apart.
[*]Older saves merge the two lists once, the first time they load. If only one list names anyone, that list is kept. If both do and they disagree, the one you could see wins: this mod's on a stand in shift use, Outfit Stands Plus's on a stand set to "Not used for shift changes". Owners you only ever set through Outfit Stands Plus are kept.
[*]On a stand set to "Not used for shift changes", Set owner now assigns one colonist at a time: choosing someone replaces whoever was listed, and Assign all is not shown. A group stand switched into that mode keeps its owners for when you switch it back, whether you used the switch or unticked its last work type, Recreation or Sleeping. Until you choose one colonist there, nobody gets the Outfit Stands Plus button for it.
[/list]
